Keep the periodic UFS I/O statistics out of the panel: they were forced
through liuqinmute, so every 1024 MiB they scrolled over the Apple logo and the
userspace boot progress bar.  They still reach the persistent console log.
---
--- a/bsd/dev/liuqin_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/liuqin_ufs.c
@@ -358,7 +358,10 @@
 		if ((st_ops & 0x3ff) == 0 && elapsed > 0) {
 			uint64_t us = elapsed / 1000;
 			extern int liuqin_console_force;
-			liuqin_console_force = 1;      /* visible even with liuqinmute=1 */
+			/* LIUQIN: keep these periodic statistics in the persistent
+			 * console log only.  Forcing them onto the panel paints over
+			 * the Apple logo and the second-boot progress bar.
+			 */
 			/* Bytes/ns * 1e9 / 2^20 is MiB/s; the old label said
 			 * KiB/s but the printed number was already MiB/s. */
 			printf("LIUQIN UFS: %llu ops, %llu MiB, %llu ms, %llu MiB/s, %llu us/op\n",
